{
  "_about": "Where each scene's subject sits, as an x centre in the 1536-pixel-wide header. derive.py cuts every derived crop around it. wide = the 2:1 social and 1.9:1 OG crops; phone = the 4:3 phone hero. Picked by eye on 2026-11-06 so Ouro and the product both stay in frame. Phone centres moved on 2026-11-06 so Ouro stands whole, tail and all, with about 96 px of scene to his right (measured from his green extent in each header); several canonical crops had him touching or past the right edge. phoneAspect (optional, default [4, 3]) widens the phone crop for a scene whose characters stand too far apart for 4:3; sites size the phone hero from the file's own width and height. A night scene (<scene>-dark) is cut with its day twin's centres; it gets its own entry only where its drawing sits differently. og (optional) moves the narrower 1.9:1 OG crop's centre on its own, where the 2:1 centre would cut a figure. wideFit \"whole\" (optional) makes the social and OG cards from the whole header under its real sky (brand/skies/<scene>.webp, from the master or an outpaint), cut to the card from the foot up, for a scene whose cast is wider than either card (render QA, 2026-11-14: these crops cut Ouro or a person at the edge). nightFromDay true (optional) builds the night twin's 4x master from this day's master given only the night header's light and colour (upscale.py, relight_transfer.py), so every large night size has the day's exact structure; set it for a night made by light transfer of its day, never for a night drawn on its own (2026-11-16: Real-ESRGAN run on day and night separately drew different texture and glyph-like specks in each). nightFromFlatDay \"flat/<scene>.webp\" (optional, instead of nightFromDay) builds it from Real-ESRGAN's 4x of that committed, flattened copy of the day (its sun pattern removed) given the night header's light and colour, for a night made by light transfer onto the flattened day: the day's 4x would bring its sun stripes back into every large night size. nightLights \"flat/<scene>-lights.png\" (optional, with nightFromFlatDay) is a header-size mask over the night's small light sources (lit lamps, glowing eyes), where the night master keeps the night header's own pixels, because they are smaller than the transfer window. nightLightsMode \"ratio\" (optional, with nightLights; default \"header\") makes the mask keep the day's 4x master times the night header's per-channel gain over the day header, upsampled and smoothed without crossing the day master's edges (a guided filter, 9 px windows at 4x), instead of the night header's own Lanczos 4x, for a mask over a lit figure or lit edge whose outline must stay as sharp as the day's (2026-11-17: ouro-md's lamp-lit head went soft and stair-stepped at 4x in the default mode). A night built from a flat day must have no hard straight step in its sky that the day doesn't explain: brand/tools/sky_seams.py checks every nightFromDay and nightFromFlatDay night's 3072 px scene in the required upscale-tests check (2026-11-18: ouro-work's flat day kept the clipped sun's flat top and a hard corner beside it, which read as a dark box in the night). cardY (optional) is a y centre in the header for the social and OG cards of a header taller than the card (a 3:2 chapter picture, 1536x1024): the card is then a full-width band around it instead of a full-height window around wide or og (default: the header's middle).",
